# Integrity gates hash artifact and config bytes FROM DISK
# (config/baseline-manifest.json -> VERIFIED_FROZEN_BASELINE). With core.autocrlf=true a
# Windows checkout rewrites LF to CRLF, so the on-disk bytes stop matching the recorded
# sha256 and the frozen-baseline gate fails even though the committed content is identical.
# Pinning these paths to LF keeps a recorded hash meaningful on every platform.
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
artifacts/** text eol=lf
config/** text eol=lf
